  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "FY27 lands on guidance (cash EBTDA ~A$340m, 21% operating margin) as US TTV grows ~30% in USD, then growth decays toward nominal GDP by FY36 as the US book matures and Pay-in-2/Stripe/Google distribution is absorbed. Group margin drifts to 23% (US already 25%, ANZ 16% improving; NZ exit removes a sub-scale drag). US net bad debts stay inside the 1.5-2.0% of TTV band and warehouse funding margins hold. Zip retains ~20c of equity per $1 of revenue growth to fund the book and returns the rest via buybacks.",
    "bull": "US embedded-finance distribution (Stripe GA, Google Pay, Visa, agentic commerce) keeps US TTV growth >30% for two more years and above 15% into FY30; scale lowers funding costs further (Nasdaq listing broadens the investor and ABS base) and operating margin climbs to 26% as fixed tech/opex is leveraged. Credit stays benign. Exit at 12x FCFE reflects a re-rating toward US BNPL peers.",
    "bear": "A US consumer-credit downturn hits Zip's low-to-middle-income, credit-constrained customer base in FY28: net bad debts break above 2% of TTV, warehouse spreads widen at renewal, management shrinks originations and margin falls to ~13% before recovering only to 17% as Afterpay/Klarna/Affirm and bank-native instalment products compress merchant take rates and the AU NCCP regime lifts compliance cost. Growth settles at 3-6%. Exit at 8x reflects a structurally lower-quality lender."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Zip is valued as a specialty lender: equity free cash flow (cash EBTDA after SBC, cash tax, capex, leases and the equity it must retain to fund receivables growth) discounted at a 13% AUD cost of equity, with warehouse/ABS debt treated as operating funding rather than net debt. Statutory history is too distorted by impairments (FY22), discontinued losses (FY23), a convertible extinguishment gain (FY24) and a DTA recognition (FY25) to extrapolate; the projection is anchored to FY27 guidance and decays to mid-cycle margins, with a heavier bear weight for credit-cycle risk.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Credit losses on a non-prime US book in a downturn (bear case margin trough ~13%)",
      "Warehouse funding cost/renewal risk; ABS spreads widen in stress",
      "Take-rate compression from Afterpay/Block, Klarna, Affirm, PayPal and bank instalment products",
      "Equity-funding share of the book (wc_capture) is estimated, not disclosed; each 5pp moves base IV ~A$0.10-0.15/share",
      "AUD/USD: ~59% of income is USD; a stronger AUD cuts reported cash EBTDA",
      "Capital-allocation risk (history of failed M&A; possible Nasdaq listing)"
    ]
  },
