    "nci_treatment": "None; wholly-owned subsidiaries.",
    "last_fcf_note": "last_fcf is a FY26 FCFE proxy, NOT reported_fcf - sbc - interest_income: cash EBTDA 268.9 - SBC 19.8 - cash tax 20.3 - capex 23.0 - lease ~5 - equity share (~10%) of the A$359m gross receivables increase ~36 = ~145. Reported OCF-less-capex (-108.9) is dominated by receivables-book funding and is not a free cash flow for a lender.",
    "notes": "MODEL: routed as a specialty consumer lender (BNPL), not an operating company. Zip funds a ~A$3.0bn receivables book with ~A$2.75bn of securitised warehouse/ABS borrowings; that debt is operating funding (its interest sits above cash EBTDA as a cost of sales), so like a bank's deposits it is NOT net debt: net_debt=0 and the flow is FCFE at cost of equity (same engine convention as NAB.AX/CHC.AX). Engine mapping: revenue = total income; 'EBITDA' = Group Cash EBTDA (after funding costs and net bad debts, before provision movement, SBC and D&A); SBC deducted explicitly; D&A for tax only; capex = PP&E + capitalised software/intangibles; working-capital capture NEGATIVE = equity Zip must retain to fund receivables growth (receivables/total income ~2.24x, ~8-11% of the book equity-funded via seller notes/first-loss and restricted cash => ~20% of each $ of revenue growth). Mid-cycle discipline: history FY21-FY23 is loss-making (FY22 A$821m impairment on failed UK/EU/Twisto/Spotii; FY23 A$41m discontinued loss), FY24 NI includes a A$139.7m convertible-note extinguishment gain and FY25 a A$54.6m DTA recognition, so no growth rate is extrapolated from statutory NI or OCF; the base path is anchored to FY27 guidance (cash EBTDA A$340m, operating margin 20-22%) and then decays. NZ wind-down (Jul-26) is small (<5% of income) and treated as immaterial. Cash tax: FY26 paid A$20.3m; tax losses largely consumed (A$98.7m left, unrecognised), so rate ramps up; path is expressed on the engine's EBIT (which is before the ~3.5%-of-revenue provision build and funding-cost amortisation), hence ~22% on engine EBIT ~ 27% blended AU30/US~25% on true PBT. Buybacks A$29.1m FY25 / A$120.9m FY26 (A$150m program complete) are a use of the FCFE the model already counts; value-neutral here. Possible Nasdaq dual listing is not modelled (no cash-flow effect; re-rating only).",
    "sanity_note": "Year-1 base: revenue ~A$1,617m, cash EBTDA ~A$340m (ties to guidance), FCFE ~A$175m => ~7% yield on ~A$2.5bn market cap.",
